# Invalid attribution: reused tool binary

The two commands exited0 but did not test chapter20. `tools/src/main.rs`
derives the repository root from compile-time `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR`, not cwd.
Reusing the chapter08 worktree binary therefore read the nine-page chapter08
registry. The command records' cwd source/registry identity must not be read
as the actual generation input identity. The manifests show nine source pages
and chapter08 Usage, with no chapter20. Both outputs and original records are
retained as a failed harness observation, not chapter20 success evidence.

The corrected invocation first builds a tool in this worktree and verifies its
manifest includes all ten registered pages. Rust code was not changed.
